{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "exportedAt": "2026-04-15T00:00:00.000Z",
  "dashboard": {
    "name": "Rule-Based Styling",
    "description": "One page per stylable chart, each with 2–3 rules across numeric, text, and parameter-reference operators and varied targets (color / backgroundColor / textColor)."
  },
  "connections": {
    "conn_postgres_read": {
      "name": "PostgreSQL Ecommerce (demo, read)",
      "type": "postgresql"
    }
  },
  "layout": {
    "version": 2,
    "pages": [
      {
        "id": "page-bar",
        "title": "1. Bar",
        "widgets": [
          {
            "id": "bar-md",
            "chartType": "markdown",
            "connectionId": "conn_postgres_read",
            "query": "",
            "settings": {
              "title": "",
              "chartOptions": {
                "content": "## Styling rules — Bar\n\nNumeric threshold rules color each bar based on its value. First matching rule wins.\n\n**Rules shown:**\n- `revenue >= 100000` → green\n- `revenue >= 50000` → amber\n- `revenue <  50000` → red (implicit — falls through to the last rule)"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "bar-chart",
            "chartType": "bar",
            "connectionId": "conn_postgres_read",
            "query": "SELECT parent.name AS category, SUM(oi.qty * oi.price)::float AS revenue FROM neoboard_demo_public.order_items oi JOIN neoboard_demo_public.products p ON p.id = oi.product_id JOIN neoboard_demo_public.categories sub ON sub.id = p.category_id JOIN neoboard_demo_public.categories parent ON parent.id = sub.parent_id GROUP BY parent.name ORDER BY revenue DESC",
            "settings": {
              "title": "Revenue by category — colored by threshold",
              "chartOptions": {
                "colorPalette": "deep-ocean",
                "showValues": true,
                "showLegend": false
              },
              "stylingConfig": {
                "enabled": true,
                "rules": [
                  {
                    "id": "bar-r1",
                    "operator": ">=",
                    "value": 100000,
                    "color": "#22c55e",
                    "target": "color"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "bar-r2",
                    "operator": ">=",
                    "value": 50000,
                    "color": "#f59e0b",
                    "target": "color"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "bar-r3",
                    "operator": "<",
                    "value": 50000,
                    "color": "#ef4444",
                    "target": "color"
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        "gridLayout": [
          { "i": "bar-md", "x": 0, "y": 0, "w": 12, "h": 3 },
          { "i": "bar-chart", "x": 0, "y": 3, "w": 12, "h": 6 }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "page-line",
        "title": "2. Line",
        "widgets": [
          {
            "id": "line-md",
            "chartType": "markdown",
            "connectionId": "conn_postgres_read",
            "query": "",
            "settings": {
              "title": "",
              "chartOptions": {
                "content": "## Styling rules — Line\n\nRules color each series based on an aggregate over its values. Useful when a chart has multiple series and you want to highlight the underperforming / leading one.\n\n**Rules shown:**\n- `revenue >= 10000` → blue\n- `revenue < 10000` → red"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "line-chart",
            "chartType": "line",
            "connectionId": "conn_postgres_read",
            "query": "SELECT to_char(date_trunc('week', created_at), 'YYYY-MM-DD') AS week, SUM(total)::float AS revenue FROM neoboard_demo_public.orders GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1",
            "settings": {
              "title": "Weekly revenue — colored by magnitude",
              "chartOptions": {
                "smooth": true,
                "area": true,
                "showLegend": true
              },
              "stylingConfig": {
                "enabled": true,
                "rules": [
                  {
                    "id": "line-r1",
                    "operator": ">=",
                    "value": 10000,
                    "color": "#2563eb",
                    "target": "color"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "line-r2",
                    "operator": "<",
                    "value": 10000,
                    "color": "#ef4444",
                    "target": "color"
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        "gridLayout": [
          { "i": "line-md", "x": 0, "y": 0, "w": 12, "h": 3 },
          { "i": "line-chart", "x": 0, "y": 3, "w": 12, "h": 6 }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "page-pie",
        "title": "3. Pie",
        "widgets": [
          {
            "id": "pie-md",
            "chartType": "markdown",
            "connectionId": "conn_postgres_read",
            "query": "",
            "settings": {
              "title": "",
              "chartOptions": {
                "content": "## Styling rules — Pie\n\nRules color each slice based on its value. Good for calling out the dominant slice or flagging unhealthy ones.\n\n**Rules shown:**\n- `value >= 400` → accent blue\n- `value <  400` → grey"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "pie-chart",
            "chartType": "pie",
            "connectionId": "conn_postgres_read",
            "query": "SELECT status AS name, COUNT(*)::float AS value FROM neoboard_demo_public.orders GROUP BY status ORDER BY value DESC",
            "settings": {
              "title": "Orders by status — highlight dominant slice",
              "chartOptions": {
                "donut": true,
                "showLegend": true
              },
              "stylingConfig": {
                "enabled": true,
                "rules": [
                  {
                    "id": "pie-r1",
                    "operator": ">=",
                    "value": 400,
                    "color": "#2563eb",
                    "target": "color"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "pie-r2",
                    "operator": "<",
                    "value": 400,
                    "color": "#94a3b8",
                    "target": "color"
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        "gridLayout": [
          { "i": "pie-md", "x": 0, "y": 0, "w": 12, "h": 3 },
          { "i": "pie-chart", "x": 2, "y": 3, "w": 8, "h": 6 }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "page-single-value",
        "title": "4. Single Value",
        "widgets": [
          {
            "id": "sv-md",
            "chartType": "markdown",
            "connectionId": "conn_postgres_read",
            "query": "",
            "settings": {
              "title": "",
              "chartOptions": {
                "content": "## Styling rules — Single Value (KPI)\n\nKPI colour encodes whether the metric is healthy. Parameter-ref comparison lets you gate styling on a dashboard-level target.\n\n**Rules shown (Delivery rate):** `>= 25%` green, `>= 15%` amber, `< 15%` red.\n\n**Rules shown (Revenue):** dynamic — `>= $param_revenue_target` blue, else grey. Change the parameter to see the color flip."
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "sv-param",
            "chartType": "parameter-select",
            "connectionId": "conn_postgres_read",
            "query": "",
            "settings": {
              "title": "Revenue target",
              "chartOptions": {
                "parameterType": "number-range",
                "parameterName": "revenue_target",
                "rangeMin": 0,
                "rangeMax": 2000000,
                "rangeStep": 50000
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "sv-delivery",
            "chartType": "single-value",
            "connectionId": "conn_postgres_read",
            "query": "SELECT (COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE status = 'delivered') * 100.0 / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0))::float AS value FROM neoboard_demo_public.orders",
            "settings": {
              "title": "Delivery rate",
              "chartOptions": {
                "suffix": "%",
                "decimalPlaces": 1,
                "fontSize": "xl"
              },
              "stylingConfig": {
                "enabled": true,
                "rules": [
                  {
                    "id": "sv-d1",
                    "operator": ">=",
                    "value": 25,
                    "color": "#22c55e",
                    "target": "color"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "sv-d2",
                    "operator": ">=",
                    "value": 15,
                    "color": "#f59e0b",
                    "target": "color"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "sv-d3",
                    "operator": "<",
                    "value": 15,
                    "color": "#ef4444",
                    "target": "color"
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "sv-revenue",
            "chartType": "single-value",
            "connectionId": "conn_postgres_read",
            "query": "SELECT SUM(total)::float AS value FROM neoboard_demo_public.orders",
            "settings": {
              "title": "Revenue vs $param_revenue_target",
              "chartOptions": {
                "prefix": "$",
                "numberFormat": "compact",
                "decimalPlaces": 1,
                "fontSize": "xl"
              },
              "stylingConfig": {
                "enabled": true,
                "rules": [
                  {
                    "id": "sv-r1",
                    "operator": ">=",
                    "value": 0,
                    "parameterRef": "revenue_target",
                    "color": "#2563eb",
                    "target": "color"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "sv-r2",
                    "operator": "<",
                    "value": 0,
                    "parameterRef": "revenue_target",
                    "color": "#94a3b8",
                    "target": "color"
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        "gridLayout": [
          { "i": "sv-md", "x": 0, "y": 0, "w": 12, "h": 4 },
          { "i": "sv-param", "x": 0, "y": 4, "w": 4, "h": 2 },
          { "i": "sv-delivery", "x": 4, "y": 4, "w": 4, "h": 3 },
          { "i": "sv-revenue", "x": 8, "y": 4, "w": 4, "h": 3 }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "page-gauge",
        "title": "5. Gauge",
        "widgets": [
          {
            "id": "gauge-md",
            "chartType": "markdown",
            "connectionId": "conn_postgres_read",
            "query": "",
            "settings": {
              "title": "",
              "chartOptions": {
                "content": "## Styling rules — Gauge\n\nGauges already support threshold zones via `chartOptions.thresholdZones`, but styling rules let you drive the needle color from the same rule engine used elsewhere.\n\n**Rules shown:**\n- `value >= 25` → green\n- `value >= 15` → amber\n- `value < 15` → red"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "gauge-chart",
            "chartType": "gauge",
            "connectionId": "conn_postgres_read",
            "query": "SELECT 'Delivered' AS name, (COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE status = 'delivered') * 100.0 / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0))::float AS value FROM neoboard_demo_public.orders",
            "settings": {
              "title": "Delivery rate — colored by threshold",
              "chartOptions": {
                "min": 0,
                "max": 100
              },
              "stylingConfig": {
                "enabled": true,
                "rules": [
                  {
                    "id": "g-r1",
                    "operator": ">=",
                    "value": 25,
                    "color": "#22c55e",
                    "target": "color"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "g-r2",
                    "operator": ">=",
                    "value": 15,
                    "color": "#f59e0b",
                    "target": "color"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "g-r3",
                    "operator": "<",
                    "value": 15,
                    "color": "#ef4444",
                    "target": "color"
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        "gridLayout": [
          { "i": "gauge-md", "x": 0, "y": 0, "w": 12, "h": 3 },
          { "i": "gauge-chart", "x": 2, "y": 3, "w": 8, "h": 6 }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "page-sunburst",
        "title": "6. Sunburst",
        "widgets": [
          {
            "id": "sb-md",
            "chartType": "markdown",
            "connectionId": "conn_postgres_read",
            "query": "",
            "settings": {
              "title": "",
              "chartOptions": {
                "content": "## Styling rules — Sunburst\n\nRules color each slice based on its value. Use `between` for band-style ranges.\n\n**Rules shown:**\n- `value >= 10000` → blue\n- `value between 2000–10000` → amber\n- `value < 2000` → red"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "sb-chart",
            "chartType": "sunburst",
            "connectionId": "conn_postgres_read",
            "query": "SELECT p.name AS name, SUM(oi.qty * oi.price)::float AS value FROM neoboard_demo_public.order_items oi JOIN neoboard_demo_public.products p ON p.id = oi.product_id GROUP BY p.id, p.name ORDER BY value DESC LIMIT 30",
            "settings": {
              "title": "Top 30 products — colored by revenue band",
              "stylingConfig": {
                "enabled": true,
                "rules": [
                  {
                    "id": "sb-r1",
                    "operator": ">=",
                    "value": 10000,
                    "color": "#2563eb",
                    "target": "color"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "sb-r2",
                    "operator": "between",
                    "value": 2000,
                    "valueTo": 10000,
                    "color": "#f59e0b",
                    "target": "color"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "sb-r3",
                    "operator": "<",
                    "value": 2000,
                    "color": "#ef4444",
                    "target": "color"
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        "gridLayout": [
          { "i": "sb-md", "x": 0, "y": 0, "w": 12, "h": 3 },
          { "i": "sb-chart", "x": 2, "y": 3, "w": 8, "h": 6 }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "page-treemap",
        "title": "7. Treemap",
        "widgets": [
          {
            "id": "tm-md",
            "chartType": "markdown",
            "connectionId": "conn_postgres_read",
            "query": "",
            "settings": {
              "title": "",
              "chartOptions": {
                "content": "## Styling rules — Treemap\n\nRectangles colored by value. Good for spotting outliers in a long-tail dataset.\n\n**Rules shown:**\n- `value >= 10000` → green\n- `value <  10000` → grey"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "tm-chart",
            "chartType": "treemap",
            "connectionId": "conn_postgres_read",
            "query": "SELECT p.name AS name, SUM(oi.qty * oi.price)::float AS value FROM neoboard_demo_public.order_items oi JOIN neoboard_demo_public.products p ON p.id = oi.product_id GROUP BY p.id, p.name ORDER BY value DESC LIMIT 30",
            "settings": {
              "title": "Top 30 products — outliers in green",
              "chartOptions": {
                "showLabels": true,
                "showValues": true
              },
              "stylingConfig": {
                "enabled": true,
                "rules": [
                  {
                    "id": "tm-r1",
                    "operator": ">=",
                    "value": 10000,
                    "color": "#22c55e",
                    "target": "color"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "tm-r2",
                    "operator": "<",
                    "value": 10000,
                    "color": "#94a3b8",
